---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Bio" description="Bio and CV">
	<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-28 pb-6 text-center">
		<h1 class="mb-6 text-[clamp(1.75rem,9vw,7rem)] font-bold uppercase tracking-tight leading-none">
			Bio
		</h1>
		<p class="mx-auto max-w-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
			Backend software engineer with strong expertise in low-latency, high-performance
			critical systems, having worked with market data applications, payment applications, and
			risk analysis software.
		</p>
		<a
			href="/curriculum.pdf"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			class="mt-8 inline-block rounded-md border border-cyan-600 px-6 py-3 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide transition-colors hover:bg-cyan-600 hover:text-white dark:border-cyan-400 dark:hover:bg-cyan-400 dark:hover:text-gray-900"
		>
			Download CV (PDF) →
		</a>

		<div class="mt-16 text-left">
			<h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight">Education</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
				MSc in Philosophy, specialization in Mathematical Logic — Unicamp (2010). Dissertation: <em
					>"On the Foundations of Paraconsistent Logic Programming"</em
				> (Portuguese: <em>"Sobre os Fundamentos da Programação Lógica Paraconsistente"</em>).
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight">Publications</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
				<li>
					Carnielli, W., Coniglio, M. E., Podiacki, R., & Rodrigues, T. (2014). <a
						href="https://doi.org/10.1017/S1755020314000148"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
						class="underline">"On the Way to a Wider Model Theory: Completeness Theorems for
						First-Order Logics of Formal Inconsistency."</a
					> <em>The Review of Symbolic Logic</em>, 7(3), 548–578.
				</li>
				<li>
					Coniglio, M. E., & Rodrigues, T. G. (2014). <a
						href="https://philpapers.org/rec/CONSIO-3"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer"
						class="underline">"Some Investigations on mbC and mCi."</a
					> In C. A. Mortari (Ed.), <em>Tópicos de lógicas não clássicas</em> (pp. 11–70). NEL/UFSC.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
